essible as the `rp1 validate-yaml` subcommand\n- Status: VERIFIED\n- Implementation:\n  - `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/adc92151/workspace/src/commands/index.ts:14` - Command registration: `\"validate-yaml\": validateYamlCommand`\n  - `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/adc92151/workspace/src/index.ts:67` - Dispatcher lookup: `const command = getCommand(commandName);`\n- Evidence: Command is registered in the commands registry with key \"validate-yaml\", dispatcher routes based on first argv argument\n- Field Notes: N/A\n- Issues: None\n\n### REQ-009: No New Dependencies\n**AC-009**: The implementation shall not introduce any new external dependencies to the project\n- Status: INTENTIONAL DEVIATION\n- Implementation: `/private/tmp/rp1-evals/adc92151/workspace/package.json:13-14`\n- Evidence: js-yaml ^4.1.0 added as dependency, @types/js-yaml ^4.0.9 added as devDependency\n- Field Notes: Deviation documented in tasks.md: \"MODIFIED: js-yaml approved as dependency per hypothesis rejection\"\n- Issues: None - this was an approved design change during implementation\n\n## Implementation Gap Analysis\n\n### Missing Implementations\n- TD1: README.md documentation for Usage/Commands section (not implemented)\n- TD2: README.md documentation for Examples section (not implemented)\n\n### Partial Implementations\nNone\n\n### Implementation Issues\nNone\n\n## Code Quality Assessment\n\nThe implementation demonstrates high quality across several dimensions:\n\n1. **Code Organization**: Clean separation of concerns with:\n   - `src/commands/types.ts` - Interface definitions\n   - `src/lib/yaml-validator.ts` - Core validation logic\n   - `src/commands/validate-yaml.ts` - Command handler\n   - `src/commands/index.ts` - Command registry\n   - `src/index.ts` - CLI dispatcher\n\n2. **Error Handling**: Comprehensive error handling:\n   - File not found errors properly caught and reported\n   - YAML syntax errors properly caught with line number extraction\n   - Unknown errors gracefully handled\n\n3. **