        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Status**: Draft\n**Created**: 2026-02-01\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nThis design implements a YAML syntax validation command integrated into the rp1 CLI. The implementation follows the commands directory pattern for extensibility, uses Bun's built-in capabilities for file operations, and leverages the `js-yaml` package that Bun bundles internally for YAML parsing.\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph CLI[\"rp1 CLI\"]\n        Entry[\"src/index.ts<br/>CLI Dispatcher\"]\n        Commands[\"src/commands/\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph ValidateYAML[\"validate-yaml Command\"]\n        Handler[\"validate-yaml.ts<br/>Command Handler\"]\n        Parser[\"YAML Parser<br/>(js-yaml)\"]\n        Formatter[\"Error Formatter\"]\n    end\n\n    User[\"User\"] -->|\"rp1 validate-yaml file.yaml\"| Entry\n    Entry -->|\"route\"| Commands\n    Commands --> Handler\n    Handler -->|\"read\"| FS[\"File System\"]\n    Handler -->|\"parse\"| Parser\n    Handler -->|\"format\"| Formatter\n    Handler -->|\"exit code + output\"| User\n```\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### 2.1 Component Architecture\n\nThe solution follows a modular command pattern with clear separation of concerns:\n\n| Component | Responsibility | Location |\n|-----------|---------------|----------|\n| CLI Dispatcher | Parse argv, route to commands, handle unknown commands | `src/index.ts` |\n| Command Interface | Define contract for all commands | `src/commands/types.ts` |\n| Validate-YAML Command | Orchestrate file validation workflow | `src/commands/validate-yaml.ts` |\n| YAML Validator | Parse YAML and extract error details | `src/lib/yaml-validator.ts` |\n\n### 2.2 Command Flow Sequence\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant Dispatcher as CLI Dispatcher\n    participant Command as validate-yaml\n    participant Validator as YAML Validator\n    participant FS as File System\n\n    User->>Dispatcher: rp1 validate-yaml file1.yaml file2.yaml\n    Dispatcher->>Dispatcher: Parse argv, identify command\n    Dispatcher->>Command: execute([\"file1.yaml\", \"file2.yaml\"])\n\n    loop For each file\n        Command->>FS: Check file exists\n        alt File not found\n            Command->>Command: Record error\n        else File exists\n            Command->>FS: Read file contents\n            Command->>Validator: validateYaml(content)\n            alt Valid YAML\n                Validator-->>Command: { valid: true }\n                Command->>Command: Record success\n            else Invalid YAML\n                Validator-->>Command: { valid: false, error, line }\n                Command->>Command: Record error with line\n            end\n        end\n    end\n\n    Command->>User: Print results for all files\n    Command->>Dispatcher: Return exit code\n    Dispatcher->>User: Exit with code (0 or 1)\n```\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 Directory Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n  index.ts                    # CLI entry point and dispatcher\n  commands/\n    types.ts                  # Command interface definition\n    validate-yaml.ts          # validate-yaml command implementation\n    index.ts                  # Command registry\n  lib/\n    yaml-validator.ts         # YAML parsing and validation logic\n```\n\n### 3.2 Interface Definitions\n\n#### Command Interface\n\n```typescript\n// src/commands/types.ts\nexport interface CommandResult {\n  exitCode: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Command {\n  name: string;\n  description: string;\n  usage: string;\n  execute(args: string[]): Promise<CommandResult>;\n}\n```\n\n#### YAML Validator Interface\n\n```typescript\n// src/lib/yaml-validator.ts\nexport interface ValidationSuccess {\n  valid: true;\n  filePath: string;\n}\n\nexport interface ValidationError {\n  valid: false;\n  filePath: string;\n  error: string;\n  line?: number;\n  column?: number;\n}\n\nexport type ValidationResult = ValidationSuccess | ValidationError;\n\nexport function validateYamlFile(filePath: string): Promise<ValidationResult>;\nexport function validateYamlContent(content: string, filePath: string): ValidationResult;\n```\n\n### 3.3 CLI Dispatcher Design\n\nThe dispatcher in `src/index.ts` will:\n\n1. Parse `process.argv` to extract command name and arguments\n2. Look up command in registry\n3. Handle `--help` flag at top level and per-command\n4. Execute command and exit with returned code\n5. Show usage for unknown commands\n\n```typescript\n// Pseudocode structure\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst commandName = args[0];\n\nif (!commandName || commandName === '--help') {\n  showGlobalHelp();\n  process.exit(0);\n}\n\nconst command = commands[commandName];\nif (!command) {\n  console.error(`Unknown command: ${commandName}`);\n  process.exit(1);\n}\n\nif (args.includes('--help')) {\n  showCommandHelp(command);\n  process.exit(0);\n}\n\nconst result = await command.execute(args.slice(1));\nprocess.exit(result.exitCode);\n```\n\n### 3.4 Validate-YAML Command Design\n\nThe command implementation handles:\n\n1. Argument validation (at least one file required)\n2. Iteration over all provided files\n3. File existence checking\n4. YAML validation via lib function\n5. Result formatting and output\n6. Exit code determination\n\n**Output Format:**\n\n```\n# Valid file:\nconfig.yaml: valid\n\n# Invalid file:\nbroken.yaml: error on line 15 - unexpected key\n\n# File not found:\nmissing.yaml: error - file not found\n\n# Summary (multiple files):\nValidated 3 files: 2 valid, 1 invalid\n```\n\n**Exit Codes:**\n- `0`: All files valid\n- `1`: One or more files invalid or not found\n\n### 3.5 YAML Validator Design\n\nUses `js-yaml` (bundled with Bun) for parsing:\n\n```typescript\nimport yaml from 'js-yaml';\n\nexport function validateYamlContent(content: string, filePath: string): ValidationResult {\n  try {\n    yaml.load(content, { filename: filePath });\n    return { valid: true, filePath };\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error instanceof yaml.YAMLException) {\n      return {\n        valid: false,\n        filePath,\n        error: error.reason || 'Invalid YAML syntax',\n        line: error.mark?.line ? error.mark.line + 1 : undefined,\n        column: error.mark?.column ? error.mark.column + 1 : undefined,\n      };\n    }\n    return {\n      valid: false,\n      filePath,\n      error: 'Unknown parsing error',\n    };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Key Design Decisions:**\n- Line numbers are 1-indexed for user display (js-yaml uses 0-indexed internally)\n- Empty files return valid (YAML spec allows empty documents)\n- Uses `yaml.load()` with safe defaults (no code execution)\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology | Rationale |\n|-------|------------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Existing project runtime |\n| Language | TypeScript | Existing project language |\n| YAML Parser | js-yaml (Bun built-in) | Bundled with Bun, no new dependency needed |\n| Testing | bun:test | Existing test framework |\n| File I/O | Bun.file() / node:fs | Native Bun APIs |\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n| # | Component | Description | Estimated Effort |\n|---|-----------|-------------|------------------|\n| T1 | Command Types | Define Command interface and types | Small |\n| T2 | YAML Validator Lib | Implement yaml-validator.ts with parsing logic | Small |\n| T3 | CLI Dispatcher | Update index.ts with command routing | Medium |\n| T4 | Validate-YAML Command | Implement the command handler | Medium |\n| T5 | Unit Tests | Tests for validator and command | Medium |\n\n## 6. Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1, T2] - Interface definitions and core validation logic have no dependencies\n2. [T3, T4] - CLI dispatcher and command can be built after interfaces defined\n3. [T5] - Tests require implementations to be complete\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T3 -> T1 (dispatcher imports Command interface)\n- T4 -> T1 (command implements Command interface)\n- T4 -> T2 (command uses yaml-validator lib)\n- T5 -> [T2, T3, T4] (tests require all implementations)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T4 -> T5\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    T1[\"T1: Command Types\"]\n    T2[\"T2: YAML Validator Lib\"]\n    T3[\"T3: CLI Dispatcher\"]\n    T4[\"T4: Validate-YAML Command\"]\n    T5[\"T5: Unit Tests\"]\n\n    T1 --> T3\n    T1 --> T4\n    T2 --> T4\n    T3 --> T5\n    T4 --> T5\n```\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### 7.1 Test Value Assessment\n\n| Test Category | Value | Rationale |\n|---------------|-------|-----------|\n| Valid YAML detection | HIGH | Core business requirement |\n| Invalid YAML with line numbers | HIGH | Core business requirement |\n| Multiple file handling | HIGH | Business rule BR-001 |\n| Exit code correctness | HIGH | CI/CD integration requirement |\n| File not found handling | MEDIUM | Error handling requirement |\n| Empty file handling | MEDIUM | Business rule BR-004 |\n| Help text display | LOW | Usability, less critical |\n\n### 7.2 Test Plan\n\n**Unit Tests (src/lib/yaml-validator.test.ts):**\n\n| Test | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| Valid simple YAML | Parse basic key-value YAML |\n| Valid complex YAML | Parse nested structures, arrays |\n| Valid empty content | Empty string returns valid |\n| Invalid syntax - missing colon | Detect and report line number |\n| Invalid syntax - bad indentation | Detect and report line number |\n| Invalid syntax - duplicate keys | Detect error |\n\n**Integration Tests (src/commands/validate-yaml.test.ts):**\n\n| Test | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| Single valid file | Returns exit code 0, prints \"valid\" |\n| Single invalid file | Returns exit code 1, prints error with line |\n| Multiple files - all valid | Returns exit code 0 |\n| Multiple files - one invalid | Returns exit code 1, validates all |\n| File not found | Returns exit code 1, prints error |\n| No arguments | Returns exit code 1, shows usage |\n\n**Test Fixtures:**\n- Create `test/fixtures/` directory with sample YAML files\n- `valid-simple.yaml` - basic valid YAML\n- `valid-complex.yaml` - nested structures\n- `invalid-syntax.yaml` - known error on specific line\n- `empty.yaml` - empty file\n\n## 8. Deployment Design\n\nNo special deployment considerations. The feature is built into the CLI:\n\n1. Code merged to main branch\n2. Standard build process (`bun build` if applicable)\n3. CLI binary includes new command automatically\n4. No configuration or environment variables required\n\n## 9. Documentation Impact\n\n| Type | Target | Section | Rationale |\n|------|--------|---------|-----------|\n| add | README.md | Usage / Commands | Document new validate-yaml command |\n| add | README.md | Examples | Show common usage patterns |\n\n## 10. Design Decisions Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|\n| D1 | CLI structure | Commands directory pattern | User preference; extensible for future commands |\n| D2 | YAML parser | js-yaml via Bun built-in | Meets no-new-deps requirement; Bun bundles it |\n| D3 | Output format | Human-readable text | Per requirements; no JSON output needed |\n| D4 | Error line numbers | 1-indexed | Standard convention for editors/IDEs |\n| D5 | Multiple file behavior | Validate all, report all | Business rule BR-001 |\n| D6 | Exit code strategy | 0 only if ALL valid | Business rule BR-002 |\n| D7 | File path resolution | Relative to CWD | Business rule BR-003, standard CLI behavior |\n"
