        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Status**: Draft\n**Created**: 2026-02-01\n\n---\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nThis design specifies a command-line YAML syntax validator implemented entirely with built-in Bun/JavaScript capabilities, without adding external dependencies. The validator reads a file, checks YAML syntax validity, and reports results with appropriate exit codes for CI/CD integration.\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    CLI[validate-yaml.ts<br/>CLI Entry Point] --> VM[yaml-validator.ts<br/>Validator Module]\n    VM --> FS[Bun.file API<br/>File System]\n    CLI --> OUT[Console Output]\n    CLI --> EXIT[Process Exit Code]\n```\n\n**Key Design Decisions:**\n- Separate CLI entry point from validation logic for testability\n- Custom minimal YAML syntax checker (no external YAML library)\n- Structured validation result type for consistent error handling\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### 2.1 Component Diagram\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TB\n    subgraph CLI Layer\n        VY[validate-yaml.ts]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Core Layer\n        YV[yaml-validator.ts]\n        subgraph Validation Functions\n            VF[validateYamlFile]\n            VS[validateYamlSyntax]\n            CH[checkIndentation]\n            CT[checkStructure]\n        end\n    end\n\n    subgraph Runtime Layer\n        BF[Bun.file API]\n        PA[process.argv]\n        PE[process.exit]\n    end\n\n    VY --> YV\n    YV --> VF\n    VF --> BF\n    VF --> VS\n    VS --> CH\n    VS --> CT\n    VY --> PA\n    VY --> PE\n```\n\n### 2.2 Sequence Diagram - Validation Flow\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant CLI as validate-yaml.ts\n    participant Val as yaml-validator.ts\n    participant FS as File System\n\n    User->>CLI: bun run validate-yaml file.yaml\n    CLI->>CLI: Parse arguments\n\n    alt No arguments\n        CLI->>User: Show usage help\n        CLI->>CLI: exit(1)\n    end\n\n    CLI->>Val: validateYamlFile(filePath)\n    Val->>FS: Bun.file(filePath).exists()\n\n    alt File not found\n        Val-->>CLI: {valid: false, error: \"File not found\"}\n        CLI->>User: Error message\n        CLI->>CLI: exit(1)\n    end\n\n    FS-->>Val: File exists\n    Val->>FS: Bun.file(filePath).text()\n    FS-->>Val: File content\n    Val->>Val: validateYamlSyntax(content)\n\n    alt Valid YAML\n        Val-->>CLI: {valid: true}\n        CLI->>User: Success message\n        CLI->>CLI: exit(0)\n    else Invalid YAML\n        Val-->>CLI: {valid: false, error, line, column}\n        CLI->>User: Error with location\n        CLI->>CLI: exit(1)\n    end\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 File Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n  validate-yaml.ts      # CLI entry point\n  yaml-validator.ts     # Validation logic module\n  yaml-validator.test.ts # Unit tests\n```\n\n### 3.2 Type Definitions\n\n```typescript\n// yaml-validator.ts\n\nexport interface ValidationResult {\n  valid: boolean;\n  error?: string;\n  line?: number;\n  column?: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ValidatorOptions {\n  allowEmpty?: boolean;  // Default: true (per BR-001)\n}\n```\n\n### 3.3 Core Functions\n\n#### validateYamlFile(filePath: string, options?: ValidatorOptions): Promise<ValidationResult>\n\nMain entry point for file validation:\n1. Check file existence using Bun.file().exists()\n2. Read file content using Bun.file().text()\n3. Call validateYamlSyntax with content\n4. Return structured result\n\n#### validateYamlSyntax(content: string, options?: ValidatorOptions): ValidationResult\n\nCore syntax validation logic:\n1. Handle empty content (valid per BR-001)\n2. Check for common YAML syntax errors:\n   - Inconsistent indentation\n   - Invalid special characters in unquoted strings\n   - Malformed key-value pairs\n   - Unclosed quotes\n   - Invalid multi-document separators\n3. Return validation result with error location if applicable\n\n### 3.4 YAML Syntax Validation Approach\n\nSince no external YAML parser is allowed, implement validation via pattern matching and structural analysis:\n\n**Validation Checks:**\n\n| Check | Description | Detection Method |\n|-------|-------------|------------------|\n| Indentation | Consistent spaces (not tabs), proper nesting | Regex + line-by-line analysis |\n| Key-Value Format | Valid `key: value` or `key:` patterns | Regex pattern matching |\n| String Quoting | Matched quotes, proper escaping | Character scanning |\n| Special Characters | Unquoted strings don't start with `@`, backtick, etc. | Regex validation |\n| Document Markers | Valid `---` and `...` usage | Line pattern matching |\n| Comments | Valid `#` comment format | Pattern matching |\n| List Items | Valid `- item` format with proper indentation | Regex + indent tracking |\n\n**Limitations (documented):**\n- Does not validate full YAML 1.2 spec compliance\n- Does not validate complex flow styles\n- Does not validate anchors/aliases\n- Focuses on common configuration file patterns\n\n### 3.5 CLI Interface\n\n```\nUsage: bun run validate-yaml <file>\n\nArguments:\n  file    Path to the YAML file to validate\n\nExit Codes:\n  0       File contains valid YAML syntax\n  1       Validation failed or error occurred\n```\n\n### 3.6 Output Format\n\n**Success:**\n```\n[OK] path/to/file.yaml is valid YAML\n```\n\n**Failure (syntax error):**\n```\n[ERROR] path/to/file.yaml\n  Line 5, Column 3: Invalid indentation - expected 2 spaces, found 3\n```\n\n**Failure (file not found):**\n```\n[ERROR] File not found: path/to/file.yaml\n```\n\n**Help (no arguments):**\n```\nYAML Validator - Validate YAML file syntax\n\nUsage: bun run validate-yaml <file>\n\nArguments:\n  file    Path to the YAML file to validate\n\nExit Codes:\n  0       File contains valid YAML syntax\n  1       Validation failed or error occurred\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technology | Rationale |\n|-------|------------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Existing project runtime |\n| Language | TypeScript | Existing project language |\n| File I/O | Bun.file API | Built-in, no deps required |\n| Testing | bun:test | Existing test framework |\n\n**No new dependencies required** - implementation uses only built-in Bun/JavaScript capabilities.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n| # | Component | Description | Effort |\n|---|-----------|-------------|--------|\n| T1 | yaml-validator.ts | Core validation module with validateYamlFile and validateYamlSyntax functions | Medium |\n| T2 | validate-yaml.ts | CLI entry point with argument parsing and output formatting | Small |\n| T3 | yaml-validator.test.ts | Unit tests for validator module | Medium |\n| T4 | package.json update | Add validate-yaml script entry | Trivial |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Core validation module, no dependencies on other new components\n2. [T2, T3] - CLI and tests both depend only on T1, can be parallel\n3. [T4] - Script entry depends on T2 existing\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface: CLI imports and uses validator module)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface: Tests import and test validator functions)\n- T4 -> T2 (Build: Script references the CLI entry point file)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4\n\n---\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### 7.1 Test Categories\n\n| Category | Target | Value |\n|----------|--------|-------|\n| Unit Tests | validateYamlSyntax function | Tests core business logic |\n| Unit Tests | validateYamlFile function | Tests file handling integration |\n| Integration Tests | CLI end-to-end | Tests full command flow |\n\n### 7.2 Test Cases\n\n**validateYamlSyntax Tests:**\n\n| Test Case | Input | Expected | Rationale |\n|-----------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| Valid simple key-value | `key: value` | valid: true | Basic YAML structure |\n| Valid nested structure | Multi-line nested YAML | valid: true | Common config pattern |\n| Valid empty file | `` (empty) | valid: true | BR-001 requirement |\n| Valid multi-document | `---\\nkey: value\\n---\\nother: value` | valid: true | BR-002 requirement |\n| Invalid indentation | Mixed tabs/spaces | valid: false, error with line | Common error |\n| Invalid key format | `key value` (no colon) | valid: false, error with line | Syntax error |\n| Unclosed quote | `key: \"unclosed` | valid: false, error | Syntax error |\n| Invalid special char | `key: @invalid` | valid: false, error | Unquoted special |\n\n**validateYamlFile Tests:**\n\n| Test Case | Input | Expected | Rationale |\n|-----------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| File not found | Non-existent path | valid: false, \"File not found\" | REQ-001 |\n| Valid file | Path to valid YAML | valid: true | REQ-002, REQ-003 |\n| Invalid file | Path to invalid YAML | valid: false with details | REQ-004 |\n\n### 7.3 Test Value Assessment\n\n| Include | Exclude |\n|---------|---------|\n| Validation logic correctness | Bun.file API behavior |\n| Error message formatting | TypeScript type checking |\n| Exit code determination | Console.log functionality |\n| Edge cases (empty, multi-doc) | File system permissions |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Deployment Design\n\n### 8.1 Script Integration\n\nAdd to package.json scripts:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"validate-yaml\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 8.2 Usage\n\n```bash\n# Direct invocation\nbun run src/validate-yaml.ts path/to/file.yaml\n\n# Via npm script\nbun run validate-yaml path/to/file.yaml\n```\n\n### 8.3 CI Integration Example\n\n```yaml\n# Example GitHub Actions step\n- name: Validate config\n  run: bun run validate-yaml config/app.yaml\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. Documentation Impact\n\n| Type | Target | Section | KB Source | Rationale |\n|------|--------|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| add | README.md | Commands/Scripts | N/A | Document new validate-yaml command usage |\n\n---\n\n## 10. Design Decisions Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| D1 | YAML parsing approach | Custom minimal syntax checker | No-dependency requirement (REQ-005) prohibits js-yaml or similar | Use js-yaml (violates req), Use JSON.parse on converted YAML (limited) |\n| D2 | Module structure | Separate validator module from CLI | Enables unit testing of logic, follows existing utils.ts pattern | Single file (less testable) |\n| D3 | Async file reading | Use async Bun.file API | Better for larger files, matches Bun idioms | Sync reading (blocks event loop) |\n| D4 | Error output format | Structured with line/column | Matches REQ-004, standard validator behavior | Simple error message only |\n| D5 | Empty file handling | Treat as valid | Explicit BR-001 requirement | Treat as invalid |\n\n---\n\n## Appendix: Flagged Assumptions\n\n| ID | Assumption | Impact | Confidence | Validation Needed |\n|----|------------|--------|------------|-------------------|\n| HYP-001 | Custom YAML syntax validation without external libraries can catch common syntax errors effectively | HIGH | LOW | Prototype validation checks against known invalid YAML samples |\n\nThis assumption is critical because YAML specification is complex. The custom validator will focus on common configuration file patterns rather than full YAML 1.2 compliance. If this proves insufficient, alternative approaches may need consideration.\n"
