        "new_string": "## Validation Findings\n\n### HYP-001 Findings\n**Validated**: 2026-02-01T03:20:00Z\n**Method**: CODE_EXPERIMENT\n**Result**: CONFIRMED\n\n**Evidence**:\n\nA prototype custom YAML validator was implemented and tested against a comprehensive test corpus. The validation was performed in multiple rounds to assess both core functionality and edge cases.\n\n**Round 1 - Core Syntax Error Detection (12 invalid files)**:\n- Tab character detection: PASS\n- Indentation jump detection: PASS\n- Missing space after colon: PASS\n- Unbalanced single quotes: PASS\n- Unbalanced double quotes: PASS\n- Odd indentation detection: PASS\n- Special character in unquoted values: PASS\n- Trailing whitespace detection: PASS\n- Special character in keys: PASS\n- Invalid line structure (missing colon): PASS\n- Mixed issues (multiple errors): PASS\n- Multiple colons detection: PASS\n\n**Result**: 12/12 invalid files correctly identified (100%)\n\n**Round 2 - False Positive Testing (10 valid files)**:\n- Simple key-value pairs: PASS (no false positive)\n- Nested structures: PASS (no false positive)\n- List items: PASS (no false positive)\n- Quoted strings with nested quotes: PASS (no false positive)\n- URLs with colons: PASS (no false positive)\n- Multiline strings: PASS (no false positive)\n- Complex nested structures: PASS (no false positive)\n- Time values with colons: PASS (no false positive)\n- Apostrophes in double quotes: PASS (no false positive)\n- Double quotes in single quotes: PASS (no false positive)\n\n**Result**: 10/10 valid files passed without false positives (100%)\n\n**Round 3 - Edge Case Analysis (15 advanced cases)**:\nTested YAML features beyond typical configuration files:\n\n| Feature | Detection Status | Notes |\n|---------|-----------------|-------|\n| Flow mapping `{key: value}` | PASS | No false positive |\n| Flow sequence `[a, b, c]` | PASS | No false positive |\n| Nested flow collections | PASS | No false positive |\n| Anchors/aliases `&` `*` | PASS | No false positive |\n| Multi-document `---` | PASS | No false positive |\n| Block chomping `|-` `>+` | PASS | No false positive |\n| Explicit types `!!type` | PASS | No false positive |\n| Unicode values | PASS | No false positive |\n| Reserved indicators (quoted) | PASS | No false positive |\n| Null/boolean variations | PASS | No false positive |\n| Number formats | PASS | No false positive |\n| Colons in values | PASS | No false positive |\n| Complex key `?` indicator | ISSUE | False positive (rare feature) |\n| Unclosed flow `{key: value` | ISSUE | Not detected (requires parsing) |\n| Duplicate keys | ISSUE | Not detected (semantic error) |\n\n**Edge Case Result**: 12/15 correct (80%)\n\n**Identified Limitations**:\n1. Complex mapping keys (`?` indicator) - rare in configuration files\n2. Flow collection brace/bracket matching - requires state machine parsing\n3. Duplicate key detection - requires semantic analysis\n4. Anchor/alias resolution validation - requires full parsing\n\n**External Research Findings**:\nAccording to industry documentation, the most common YAML syntax errors in configuration files are:\n1. **Indentation errors** (~70% of issues) - Prototype handles these\n2. **Tab vs space issues** (~37% of structure issues) - Prototype handles these\n3. **Special character quoting** - Prototype handles these\n4. **Improper list/quote usage** - Prototype handles these\n\nFlow style (JSON-like syntax) is discouraged in most style guides. Home Assistant documentation explicitly states \"Flow style is not allowed.\" Most configuration files use block style exclusively, where the prototype excels.\n\n**Sources**:\n- Prototype code: `/tmp/hypothesis-yaml-validator/yaml-validator-v2.ts`\n- Edge case analysis: `/tmp/hypothesis-yaml-validator/yaml-validator-v3-edge-cases.ts`\n- https://moldstud.com/articles/p-yaml-errors-demystified-common-mistakes-and-solutions-explained\n- https://developers.home-assistant.io/docs/documenting/yaml-style-guide/\n- https://www.devopsroles.com/fix-syntax-error-while-loading-yaml-in-ansible/\n\n**Implications for Design**:\n\n1. **Feasibility Confirmed**: A custom pattern-based YAML validator CAN effectively catch the most common syntax errors (indentation, tabs, quoting, key-value format, special characters) that account for the vast majority of real-world YAML configuration issues.\n\n2. **Scope Recommendation**: The validator should focus on block-style YAML validation, which is the standard for configuration files. Flow style validation is complex and rarely needed.\n\n3. **Known Limitations to Document**:\n   - Cannot validate flow collection syntax (unclosed braces/brackets)\n   - Cannot detect duplicate keys (semantic error)\n   - Cannot validate anchor/alias references\n   - Complex mapping keys (`?` indicator) may produce false positives\n\n4. **User Guidance**: Documentation should note that the validator catches syntax errors but is not a full YAML parser. Users with advanced YAML features should use a full parser for comprehensive validation.\n\n5. **Implementation Approach**: The ~150-line prototype demonstrates the core validation logic is straightforward to implement without dependencies, covering:\n   - Tab detection\n   - Indentation consistency checking\n   - Quote balance tracking (with nested quote support)\n   - Colon placement validation\n   - Structure validation (key-value vs list items)\n   - Special character detection\n   - Trailing whitespace detection\n\n## Summary\n| Hypothesis | Risk | Result | Implication |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------|\n| HYP-001 | HIGH | CONFIRMED | Custom YAML validation is feasible for common syntax errors; document known limitations for advanced features |\n"
