        "content": "# Design Decisions: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Created**: 2026-02-01\n\n## Decision Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| D1 | YAML parsing approach | Custom minimal syntax checker | No-dependency requirement (REQ-005) prohibits js-yaml or similar external libraries. Must rely solely on built-in JavaScript/Bun capabilities. | 1. Use js-yaml package (violates no-deps requirement), 2. Use yaml package (violates no-deps), 3. Convert to JSON and use JSON.parse (limited YAML support) |\n| D2 | Module structure | Separate yaml-validator.ts from validate-yaml.ts CLI | Enables isolated unit testing of validation logic without CLI concerns. Follows existing codebase pattern (utils.ts separate from index.ts). | Single file combining CLI and logic (harder to test, violates separation of concerns) |\n| D3 | File reading approach | Async using Bun.file().text() | Better performance for larger files, non-blocking, matches idiomatic Bun patterns. | Synchronous file reading (blocks event loop, not recommended for potentially large files) |\n| D4 | Error output format | Structured with line number and column when available | Meets REQ-004 requirement for actionable error information. Standard behavior for validation tools. | Simple error message without location (less useful for debugging) |\n| D5 | Empty file handling | Treat as valid YAML | Explicit business rule BR-001 specifies empty files are valid YAML (empty document). | Treat empty as invalid (contradicts requirement) |\n| D6 | Multi-document handling | Validate entire file including document separators | BR-002 requires multi-document files (---) to be validated as a whole. | Validate only first document (incomplete), Split and validate separately (more complex) |\n| D7 | Exit codes | 0 for valid, 1 for invalid/error | Standard Unix convention, suitable for CI/CD integration per REQ-003/REQ-004. | Custom exit codes for different error types (unnecessary complexity) |\n| D8 | Test file location | Colocated as yaml-validator.test.ts | Follows existing project pattern (utils.test.ts next to utils.ts). | Separate test directory (inconsistent with project) |\n| D9 | Script naming | validate-yaml | Descriptive, follows kebab-case pattern used in existing scripts (e.g., no camelCase). | yaml-validate, validateYaml, check-yaml |\n| D10 | Validation scope | Common configuration file patterns only | Full YAML 1.2 spec is extremely complex. Focus on patterns developers actually use in config files. Custom validator cannot reasonably implement full spec. | Attempt full YAML spec (not feasible without library), Very minimal checks only (insufficient value) |\n\n## AFK Mode: Auto-Selected Technology Decisions\n\n| Decision | Choice | Source | Rationale |\n|----------|--------|--------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Codebase analysis | Project uses Bun runtime exclusively (package.json scripts use bun) |\n| Language | TypeScript | Codebase analysis | All source files are .ts, tsconfig.json configured |\n| Test framework | bun:test | Codebase analysis | Existing tests use bun:test (src/utils.test.ts) |\n| File I/O API | Bun.file() | Codebase analysis + default | Bun's native file API, matches runtime |\n| Module format | ES Modules | Codebase analysis | package.json has \"type\": \"module\" |\n| CLI argument parsing | process.argv | Codebase analysis | Existing index.ts uses process.argv[2] pattern |\n| YAML library | None (custom) | Requirements | REQ-005 explicitly prohibits new dependencies |\n\n## Assumptions Requiring Validation\n\n| ID | Assumption | Impact if Wrong | Confidence | Recommended Action |\n|----|------------|-----------------|------------|-------------------|\n| HYP-001 | Custom YAML syntax validation can effectively detect common syntax errors without using an external YAML parser library | HIGH - Feature may not provide meaningful validation value | LOW - YAML spec is complex, unclear if pattern-based approach is sufficient | Test prototype against corpus of known-invalid YAML files before finalizing implementation |\n\n## Design Constraints Applied\n\n| Constraint | Source | Impact on Design |\n|------------|--------|------------------|\n| No new npm dependencies | REQ-005 | Cannot use js-yaml, yaml, or any external YAML parsing library. Must implement custom validation. |\n| TypeScript required | Requirements section 9 | Implementation in TypeScript, using existing tsconfig.json settings |\n| Bun runtime | Existing project | Use Bun-specific APIs (Bun.file), bun:test for testing |\n| Must follow existing patterns | Project structure | Colocated tests, similar module structure to utils.ts/index.ts |\n"
