        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 5 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 2 days\n**Started**: 2026-02-01\n\n## Overview\n\nA command-line YAML syntax validator implemented using built-in Bun/JavaScript capabilities without external dependencies. The validator reads a file, checks YAML syntax validity, and reports results with appropriate exit codes for CI/CD integration.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Core validation module, no dependencies on other new components\n2. [T2, T3] - CLI and tests both depend only on T1, can be parallel\n3. [T4] - Script entry depends on T2 existing\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (Interface: CLI imports and uses validator module)\n- T3 -> T1 (Interface: Tests import and test validator functions)\n- T4 -> T2 (Build: Script references the CLI entry point file)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T4\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Core Foundation\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Implement yaml-validator.ts core validation module with ValidationResult interface and validation functions `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#3-detailed-design](design.md#3-detailed-design)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] ValidationResult interface defined with valid, error, line, and column fields\n    - [ ] ValidatorOptions interface defined with allowEmpty option\n    - [ ] validateYamlFile function implemented using Bun.file API for existence check and content reading\n    - [ ] validateYamlSyntax function implements pattern-based validation for indentation, key-value format, string quoting, special characters, document markers, comments, and list items\n    - [ ] Empty files return valid: true per BR-001\n    - [ ] Multi-document files (with ---) validated as a whole per BR-002\n    - [ ] Error results include line and column information when applicable\n\n### CLI and Testing\n\n- [ ] **T2**: Implement validate-yaml.ts CLI entry point with argument parsing and output formatting `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#35-cli-interface](design.md#35-cli-interface)\n\n    **Effort**: 2 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] CLI accepts file path as command-line argument via process.argv\n    - [ ] Shows usage help when no arguments provided\n    - [ ] Outputs \"[OK] path/to/file.yaml is valid YAML\" on success\n    - [ ] Outputs \"[ERROR] path/to/file.yaml\" with line/column details on syntax failure\n    - [ ] Outputs \"[ERROR] File not found: path/to/file.yaml\" when file missing\n    - [ ] Exits with code 0 on valid YAML\n    - [ ] Exits with code 1 on validation failure or error\n\n- [ ] **T3**: Implement yaml-validator.test.ts unit tests for validator module `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#7-testing-strategy](design.md#7-testing-strategy)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Test valid simple key-value YAML returns valid: true\n    - [ ] Test valid nested structure YAML returns valid: true\n    - [ ] Test empty file returns valid: true per BR-001\n    - [ ] Test multi-document YAML returns valid: true per BR-002\n    - [ ] Test invalid indentation returns valid: false with error and line info\n    - [ ] Test invalid key format (missing colon) returns valid: false with error and line info\n    - [ ] Test unclosed quote returns valid: false with error\n    - [ ] Test invalid special character in unquoted string returns valid: false with error\n    - [ ] Test file not found returns valid: false with \"File not found\" error\n    - [ ] Test valid file path returns appropriate validation result\n    - [ ] Test invalid file path returns error with details\n\n### Integration\n\n- [ ] **T4**: Update package.json to add validate-yaml script entry `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#81-script-integration](design.md#8